The '''2016 FA Community Shield''' (also known as '''The FA Community Shield supported by [[McDonald's]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 94th [[FA Community Shield]], an annual English [[association football|football]] match played between the winners of the previous season's [[Premier League]] and [[FA Cup]]. The match was contested by [[2015–16 FA Cup]] winners [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]], and [[Leicester City F.C.|Leicester City]], champions of the [[2015–16 Premier League]]. It was held at [[Wembley Stadium]] a week before the [[2016–17 Premier League|Premier League season]] kicked off. Manchester United won the match 2–1 with goals from [[Jesse Lingard]] and [[Zlatan Ibrahimović]], either side of a goal from Leicester striker [[Jamie Vardy]].

[[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] were the holders, having won the [[2015 FA Community Shield|2015 edition]], but did not qualify for this match, as they finished second in the [[2015–16 Premier League|Premier League]] and got knocked out of the [[2015–16 FA Cup|FA Cup]] in the sixth round.

==Background==
Leicester City qualified as champions of the [[2015–16 Premier League]]. They won the title after then-second place [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]] drew 2–2 to [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] in [[Stamford Bridge (stadium)|Stamford Bridge]] on 2 May 2016. It was only their second FA Charity/Community Shield, first since [[1971 FA Charity Shield|1971]], when they defeated [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] 1–0. It was also the first time they played as champions/runners–up of either top division league or FA Cup winners, as they played in 1971 as Second Division champions.

Manchester United qualified as winners of the [[2015–16 FA Cup]]. They defeated [[Crystal Palace F.C.|Crystal Palace]] [[2016 FA Cup final|2–1]] after extra time on 21 May 2016 to win their 12th title (tying the then-record with [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]]). It was their 30th FA Charity/Community Shield, winning a record 20.

The previous match between the two sides was a 1–1 draw at [[Old Trafford]] on 1 May 2016. [[Anthony Martial]] scored for United in the eighth minute, while Leicester captain [[Wes Morgan]] equalised nine minutes later.

Manchester United manager [[José Mourinho]] returned to the Community Shield for the second straight year, after managing for [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] in the [[2015 FA Community Shield]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2016/aug/07/leicester-city-v-manchester-united-community-shield-live|title=Leicester 1 Man Utd 2|date=7 August 2016|work=Guardian|access-date=9 August 2016}}</ref>

==Match==
===Summary===
[[Jesse Lingard]] opened the scoring in the 32nd minute when he ran and got past three Leicester players before shooting low with his right foot past the onrushing Leicester goalkeeper [[Kasper Schmeichel]] who managed to get something on the shot but could not prevent it going into the net.<ref>{{cite web|url= http://www.the42.ie/leicester-city-manchester-united-live-2914735-Aug2016/|title=Community Shield: Leicester City 1 Manchester United 2 as it happened|date=7 August 2016|work=The 42|access-date=23 February 2017}}</ref> [[Jamie Vardy]] made it 1–1 in the 52nd minute when he intercepted [[Marouane Fellaini]]'s no-look back-pass before rounding [[David de Gea]] and slotting the ball low to the net with his left foot.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2016/08/07/manchester-united-vs-leicester-city-community-shield-live-score/ |title=Community Shield: Leicester City 1 Manchester United 2 - Zlatan Ibrahimovic late header wins United's 21st Shield |date=7 August 2016 |work=Telegraph |access-date=23 February 2017 }}</ref> [[Zlatan Ibrahimović]] got the winning goal for Manchester United in the 83rd minute when he got above Leicester captain [[Wes Morgan]] and headed in from six yards out into the right corner off the post after a cross from the right by [[Antonio Valencia]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/aug/07/leicester-city-manchester-united-community-shield-match-report |title=Community Shield: Manchester United beat Leicester with Ibrahimovic header |date=7 August 2016 |work=Guardian |access-date=23 February 2017 }}</ref>

